title: Sequence Diagram
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki
tags: MermaidExample

A sequence diagram shows messages exchanged between participants over time, in left-to-right order. Use it for API interactions, authentication flows, protocol design, and actor communication. Uses `sequenceDiagram`.

---

!! Basic example

```
sequenceDiagram
    participant Alice
    participant Bob
    Alice->>Bob: Hello Bob
    Bob-->>Alice: Hi Alice!
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant Alice
    participant Bob
    Alice->>Bob: Hello Bob
    Bob-->>Alice: Hi Alice!
$$$

---

!! Real-world example: OAuth2 authorization code flow

This example shows a browser-based OAuth2 login: the user's browser redirects to the authorization server, receives a code, and exchanges it for an access token. Activation bars show which participant is processing at each step.

```
%%{init: {"sequence": {"showSequenceNumbers": true}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: OAuth2 authorization code flow
    accDescr: Browser login via OAuth2 with token exchange

    %% ── Participants ────────────────────────────
    participant Browser
    participant AppServer as App Server
    participant AuthServer as Auth Server
    participant ResourceServer as Resource Server

    %% ── Step 1: Redirect to Auth Server ─────────
    Browser->>AppServer: GET /login
    activate AppServer
    AppServer-->>Browser: 302 Redirect to /authorize
    deactivate AppServer

    %% ── Step 2: User authenticates ──────────────
    Browser->>AuthServer: GET /authorize?client_id=...
    activate AuthServer
    AuthServer-->>Browser: Login page
    Browser->>AuthServer: POST credentials
    AuthServer-->>Browser: 302 Redirect with ?code=xyz
    deactivate AuthServer

    %% ── Step 3: Code exchange ────────────────────
    Browser->>AppServer: GET /callback?code=xyz
    activate AppServer
    AppServer->>AuthServer: POST /token (code + secret)
    activate AuthServer
    AuthServer-->>AppServer: access_token + refresh_token
    deactivate AuthServer

    %% ── Step 4: Access protected resource ────────
    AppServer->>ResourceServer: GET /api/user (Bearer token)
    activate ResourceServer
    ResourceServer-->>AppServer: 200 User profile JSON
    deactivate ResourceServer
    AppServer-->>Browser: 200 User dashboard
    deactivate AppServer

    %% ── Error path ───────────────────────────────
    alt Token expired
        Browser->>AppServer: GET /refresh
        AppServer->>AuthServer: POST /token (refresh_token)
        AuthServer-->>AppServer: new access_token
    end
```

$$$text/vnd.tiddlywiki.mermaid
