---

!! Syntax

```
sequenceDiagram
    participant A as Display Name
    A->>B: Synchronous message
    A-->>B: Response (dashed)
    activate B
    B-->>A: reply
    deactivate B

    loop Retry
        A->>B: try again
    end

    alt Success
        B-->>A: 200 OK
    else Error
        B-->>A: 500 Error
    end
```

|!Arrow|!Meaning|
|`->>`|Synchronous (solid, filled arrowhead)|
|`-->>`|Response (dashed, filled arrowhead)|
|`->>`|Open arrowhead variant|
|`-x`|Cross/terminate|
|`-)`|Async (open arrowhead)|

!! Tips

* `participant A as Display Name` shows a shorter ID in the source but a human-readable label in the diagram.
* `activate`/`deactivate` draw activation bars on a participant's lifeline.
* Use `alt`/`else`/`end` for conditional branches; `loop`/`end` for repetition; `opt`/`end` for optional steps.
* `%%{init: {"sequence": {"showSequenceNumbers": true}}}%%` numbers each message automatically.
* Sequence diagrams do not use `classDef` — there is no color-category legend for this type.
* See also: [[Flowchart]] for process flows, [[State Diagram]] for state machines.

